The furthest I have ever gotten with a character was the first level
of Gehennom.  This valk had made the stupid mistake of self-genocide.

The furthest I have ever gotten a wizard was up to level 14.  This
wizard foolishly attacked the priest at minetown, and got whooped with
the help of lycanthropy (I should of had that cloak of MR on)

But this is the first time I have beaten the game.

eliotn traveled with her cat Toddfujawa through the Dungeons of Doom.
An altar on level 4 was a boon.  After going to level 9 (oracle
level), she turned around, since telepathy had detected a gargoyle.
She camped at an altar and repeatedly sacrificed until Anhur was happy
with a lizard corpse. She recieved Magicbane for her troubles, which
turned out to be a lifesaver.  Unfortunately, Toddfujawa got killed by
a panther.

Eliotn also had a near-death experience.  She was near one of the
demon lords (sacrificing elves), and was confused and low on hp.
Desperate, she read a scroll, which turned out to be a scroll of
taming...

After finding out that a lamp on the Oracle level was magical and
contained a genie, she repeatedly rubbed the lamp until the genie came
out and gave her a wish.  She wished for a +2 SDSM, which proved to be
really useful.

Sokoban yielded her a bag of holding; another useful item.  Then, with
two new pets, she descended into the mines...

The mines were a piece of cake, except that one of my pets died to a
gnome with a wand of striking.  A bones file gave me a helm of
brilliance, among other things, and a new pet to tame.

I went into the wine cellar version of Mine's End.  After getting to
the luckstone, I noticed something odd.  What is a baby red dragon
doing here?  I then noticed that there was a polymorph trap in the
room.  Happy, I polymorphed one pet (the bones one) into a vampire
lord and I polymorphed the other pet into a marillith.

I was anxious to go on the quest.  However, an experience level of 11
would not suffice.  I danced on a magic trap.  Killing enemies raised
my experience level to  level 12.  I then went to the quest level.
With some advice, I began to create monsters on the quest level,
hoping that one of these would be a wraith.  With no success, I left
the quest level and explored more of the dungeon.  I found a potion of
gain level, so I blessed it and went to level 13.  After turning
around and heading back to the quest level, I noticed that I was very
close to leveling up.  I created monsters and killed them.
Ironically, I stepped on a magic trap and a wraith appeared; I ate its
corpse to reach level 14.

The quest wasn't too difficult.  I ate tengu on the quest to get the
teleport and teleport control instrincs.  Unfortunately, I lost the
vampire lord when I fell through a trapdoor (but the marillith had
reached the level)  The hard part was the nemesis, which I found to be
a challenging fight.  He was so annoying!  Lord Surtur was a piece of
cake, but the dark one kept teleporting, casting spells at me, and
even escaped upstairs.  I shot a wand of death... no effect on him.  I
hoped that my pet would help me kill the nemesis, but the pet was
still helpful as it took care of the other monster.

Finally, I killed him, and received a massive boon: the Eye of the
Aethiopica.  This item became one of the most useful items I gained.
After getting back to the altar, I blessed and drank a potion of gain
level.  Instead, a genie came out and I wished for an uncursed magic
marker.  With it, I genocided L and h, and enchanted my armor up too.

I brought my stash to the first level of sokoban, and went to the
Valley of the Dead.  Then, I went to the Castle, sneaking through the
back.  With my improved mana regeneration, the castle was a piece of
cake.  I quickly went to the chest with the wand of wishing.
Receiving it, I noticed that I had already called it "no message".
This meant I had another wand in my stash.  Going back to my stash, I
found that wand of wishing and found that it only had one charge
left.  I wrested it and wished for another uncursed magic marker.

After asking for advice, I wished for a pair of speed boots.  A
rothe's death drop also provided me with gauntlets of dexterity.
Also, I wrote a spellbook of identify, which turned out to help me
find out what cool rings I had.  After enchanting up my armor, I went
back to the castle and decided to get a good pet.

With a figurine I found from polypilling, I went to the polymorph trap
in the mines and got a purple worm on the first polymorph.  Then,  the
purple worm ate a chameleon corpse and turned into a rothe.  So I had
to polymorph it some more until I got a baby purple worm.  It was
weak, though.

After seeing a real purple worm, I decided I wanted to tame it.  I
levelported back to my stash and wished up another uncursed magic
marker.  With this, I wrote a spellbook of charm monster.  Then, after
deciding that I wanted to polypile some stuff, I also wished for a
blessed spellbook of polymorph.

Around this time, I also camped at an altar, sacrificing and praying,
until I get crowned.  This gave me useful instrincs and the finger of
death spell.  I also sacrificed an elf corpse, and summoned a
foocubus.  This really helped me level up.

Polymorph helped me out the most when I wanted an amulet of life
saving.  I blessed and polypiled those amulets, and some of them did
yield amulets of life saving (I had 5 by the time I ascended).
Ironically, I never needed to use them).

I also wished for a cursed magic marker, and wrote 3 cursed scrolls of
genocide with it.  I used one to nurse dance now, one to summon
wraiths, and one to nurse dance at my last visit to the stash.  I also
polymorphed into a cockatrice in order to lay eggs, but I only used
two of them.

I soon found out that purple worms were not as strong as I thought,
since the purple worm quickly got killed by monsters.

I dug out paths between levels, then went to Gehennom.  It was quick.
I didn't bother with finding stuff, I just magic mapped, dug a path
between the stairs, and went down.  I stoned Orcus with one of the
cockatrice eggs.  Vlad was an easy  kill with magic missile.  I found
another foocubus, which also helped.

With one last visit to my stash, I took most of the items you see
here.  I dug down to the last level, found the vibrating square (took
some time), and prepared to face Rodney.

After finding the portal, a cockatrice within the tower proved a
powerful weapon as I stoned lots of monsters and Rodney with it.  I
grabed the book and levelported to the last level.  After teleporting
to the vibrating square, I preformed the invocation and levelported to
the last level.  With my cockatrice corpse, I stoned all of the
monsters and the high priest, and took the Amulet.

The ascention run was easy.  The only time Rodney showed up was at the
plane of Earth.  I was prepared, however, and I stoned him with
another cockatrice egg.

On the plane of air, the only trouble was the air elementals, but
finger of death took care of them.

Nothing bothered me on fire and water.  I wished for a cockatrice
corpse on astral, and cleared out the monsters with it.  The first
altar was coaligned, so I sacrificed the Amulet of Yendor to Anhur.

eliotn, chaotic female elven Wizard



